From 3317e94de2334374f211a9b9bde68bba6e721eaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "William Mark Katzenmeyer, P.E., C.F.M." <heccommander@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:17:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] hdf5-reader: sparse row/column gathers and uncached
 full reads

[L06] Status vs upstream v0.9.3: NOT UPSTREAM.
Kind: performance + API. Proposed upstream grouping: PR-C performance/API (engine-shaped; discuss first).
Applies on roteiro-gis/netcdf-rust v0.9.3 (3d708fd) after the earlier patches of this series.

Add Dataset::read_rows_columns_chunked (and, with the rayon feature,
read_rows_columns_chunked_parallel and read_rows_columns_chunked_in_pool):
read a strided row range and an ordered, possibly repeated column list of
a 2-D chunked dataset with one bounded chunk-index traversal and per-chunk
compact gathers, without materialising the full row slab. Returns
Ok(None) for layouts it does not handle so callers can fall back.

Add Dataset::read_array_uncached(_parallel): a full read that neither
inserts nor evicts cached chunks nor retains the hot-array copy. A chunk
cache of zero bytes now bypasses the cache entirely, and
ChunkCache::capacity_bytes, DEFAULT_CHUNK_CACHE_BYTES and
DEFAULT_CHUNK_CACHE_SLOTS are exposed.

Adds tests/fixtures/perf2/gather.h5.
